[{"text":"d6 · π71 (8, 0) · π70 (14, 1) · 1","section":"All differentials (“low”), n≤83"},{"text":"d6 · π81 (10, 0) · π80 (16, 1) · 1","section":"All differentials (“low”), n≤83"},{"text":"d6 · π82 (5, 0) · π81 (11, 1) · 1","section":"All differentials (“low”), n≤83"},{"text":"The full list up to n=150 is in differentials.json.","section":"All differentials (“low”), n≤83"},{"text":"For n≤82 the rule disagrees with Toda in π49, π50, π51, π59, π60, π63, π64, π66, π67, π68, π69, π70, π73, π74, π75, π76, π77, π79, π80. Almost all of the extra classes are removed by arrows d5 that do not change the colour; at p=3 this is d2p-1, the length of Toda's differential. Allowing such d5 in addition to the rule (with the same greedy filling) gives the following d5:","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"from (s, c) · to (s, c) · rank","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π50 (5, 0) · π49 (10, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π51 (5, 1) · π50 (10, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π58 (5, 0) · π57 (10, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π60 (7, 0) · π59 (12, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π61 (7, 1) · π60 (12, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π68 (7, 0) · π67 (12, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π70 (9, 0) · π69 (14, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π71 (9, 1) · π70 (14, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π74 (6, 1) · π73 (11, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π76 (7, 0) · π75 (12, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π77 (7, 1) · π76 (12, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π78 (9, 0) · π77 (14, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π80 (11, 0) · π79 (16, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π82 (5, 0) · π81 (10, 0) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"d5 · π81 (11, 1) · π80 (16, 1) · 1","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"Disagreements remain in π57, π58, π63, π64, π66, π67, π73, π74, π75, π76, π78, π79, π80: there the greedy d5 kills classes that are alive in Toda. So Toda needs some colour-preserving d5, but not all the allowed ones. None of the purely colour-based variants we checked reproduces Toda beyond π48.","section":"What the rule is missing"},{"text":"differentials.json","section":"What the rule is missing"}]